  "headline": "Calcium chloride is not on FDA's shortage list; Hospira's product is marked To Be Discontinued as of 2025-11-07",
  "headline_cites": ["D3", "E16"],
  "sentences": [
    {
      "text": "FDA's drug shortage list does not include calcium chloride as of 2026-10-21.",
      "cites": ["D3"]
    },
    {
      "text": "Hospira, Inc., a Pfizer Company, has a calcium chloride injection entry on the shortage list with status To Be Discontinued and an initial posting date of 2025-11-07.",
      "cites": ["E16"]
    },
    {
      "text": "The label for NDC 00409163110 names Hospira, Inc. as the registered plant (FEI 1021343) with a last inspection classified NAI on 2025-02-07.",
      "cites": ["E15"]
    },
    {
      "text": "FDA inspection records for that plant show multiple OAI classifications in 2010 and 2011, followed by VAI classifications through 2019.",
      "cites": ["E5", "E7", "E9", "E10", "E11", "E12", "E13"]
    },
    {
      "text": "A Warning Letter was issued to Hospira, Inc. on 2010-04-12.",
      "cites": ["E14"]
    },
    {
      "text": "The top-ranked purchasing option is to buy from American Regent, Inc., which is not on FDA's shortage list today.",
      "cites": ["D4"]
    },
    {
      "text": "Corvale East has 29.4 days on hand and Corvale General has 16.2 days on hand for the 100 mg/mL 10 mL syringe presentation.",
      "cites": ["D1", "D2"]
    }
  ]
}
